1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/a> <\/p>\n<h2>Getting there<\/h2>\n<h3>Train connections<\/h3>\n<p>The central station of Antwerp is the main gate to the city. It is well connected with high-speed lines. Amsterdam, Brussels, Lille, and Paris have direct high-speed connections. In Brussels, connections can be made with the high-speed lines to London, Cologne and Berlin. <\/p>\n<h3>Airports<\/h3>\n<p>Antwerp Airport (IATA: ANR): <a href=\"http:\/\/www.antwerp-airport.com\/\" title=\"http:\/\/www.antwerp-airport.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><\/a> (10 min from the city center)<br \/>\nBrussels Airport (IATA: BRU): <a href=\"https:\/\/www.brusselsairport.be\" title=\"https:\/\/www.brusselsairport.be\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><\/a> (30-45 min by train)<br \/>\nAmsterdam Airport (IATA: AMS): <a href=\"https:\/\/www.schiphol.nl\" title=\"https:\/\/www.schiphol.nl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><\/a> (55 min by high-speed train, 1,5h-2h regular trains )<\/p>\n<p>NB the central train station has an IATA code: ZWE. With some airlines, this allows having the train station as a final destination as part of the total booking.<br \/>\n <a href=\"https:\/\/www.klm.com\/travel\/be_en\/plan_and_book\/ticket_information\/travel_by_train_on_a_klm_ticket\/index.htm#p4\" title=\"https:\/\/www.klm.com\/travel\/be_en\/plan_and_book\/ticket_information\/travel_by_train_on_a_klm_ticket\/index.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><\/a> <\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Venue SWAT4HCLS 2018 will be held in Antwerp, Belgium. The venue will be at Elzenveld, a historic building that served as hospital and monastery. Getting there Train connections The central station of Antwerp is the main gate to the city. &hellip; <a href=\"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/workshops\/antwerp2018\/venue-and-useful-information\/\">Continue reading <span class=\"meta-nav\">&rarr;<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featu